Protect Democracy seeks a thoughtful, detail-oriented fundraiser to join our growing Partnerships team as an Annual Giving Officer. This is a unique opportunity for a talented early-to-mid-career fundraising professional looking to expand their skill set and make an impact in the movement to protect our democracy. As Annual Giving Officer, you’ll steward a portfolio of mid-level donors and run the engagement tools to grow it, including across our grassroots and peer-to-peer fundraising programs.
About the position: In this role, you’ll be a key player on a small, highly collaborative and effective team. We seek to steward deep, long-term, trusting relationships with donors, engaging them as true partners in the broader democracy ecosystem. That approach has paid off: We’ve raised substantial unrestricted operating funds and built a solid financial runway, which lets us hire exceptional talent and launch high-impact interventions. These include 150+ legal actions, critical federal and state legislation, and creative solutions like VoteShield, which monitors and protects 160 million public voter records across 25 states.
About the organization: Protect Democracy formed in late 2016, recognizing that the global wave of authoritarianism had begun to erode American shores . We have since assembled a team of 140+ experts who have served under Democrats and Republicans and in the senior ranks of other nonprofit, political, or media organizations. Our team includes lawyers, policy experts, legislative advocates, media strategists, writers, data analysts, and software developers. We deploy litigation, legislative and communications strategies, technology, research, and analysis to stand up for free and fair elections, the rule of law, fact-based debate, and a better democracy for future generations. For this work, our team received a Skoll Award for Social Innovation and a MacArthur Fellowship .
This is a remote position based in the United States.* The priority deadline to apply for this role is October 29, 2026; we will review applications received after that date on a rolling basis.
The Annual Giving Officer will:

• Manage a portfolio that currently has about 300 mid level gift partners-both institutional funders and individuals-leveraging technology to assist in regular communications, soliciting gift renewals, and customized cultivation plans where appropriate;

• Aim to grow this portfolio of donors to 500 by 2028 through strong collaboration with Partnerships team members, active stewardship, and management of our newly launched peer-to-peer fundraising tool;

• Write & distribute high-quality quarterly e-newsletter & bi-annual e-appeals to grassroots donors, mostly through synthesis of existing material;

• Assemble high-quality materials and communications that reflect Protect Democracy ’s voice and mission, including grant proposals, reports, and donor correspondence;

• Represent Protect Democracy in external meetings with donors and trusted intermediaries;

• Conduct prospect research to identify new high-capacity individuals and institutions aligned with our mission;

• Collaborate with the Partnerships team to set and track ambitious fundraising goals, maintaining accurate and up-to-date records;

• Independently seek opportunities to build and improve on Protect Democracy ’s fundraising operations by closely examining needs, assessing possible solutions, and making concise recommendations;

• Contribute to Protect Democracy ’s programmatic work and culture.

The ideal candidate brings:

• Three or more years of professional experience, including experience working directly with donors;

• Demonstrated comfort and experience with identifying, cultivating, stewarding, closing, and renewing 4-5 figure gift opportunities;

• Proficiency with fundraising tools and CRMs with a preference for Raiser’s Edge experience, and a desire to help our team use data and automation more effectively;

• Ability to correspond persuasively

About MPU

More Perfect Union is an advocacy, journalism, and education organization with a mission to build power for the working class. Since launching in February 2021, More Perfect Union’s Emmy award-winning coverage has garnered 8 million followers and subscribers. We are the fastest growing news/politics YouTube channel.

About the Position

We are hiring a creative and detail-oriented Social Media Fellow to join our social media team and help us to engage and grow our audience on a daily basis. This is a remote, 6 month fellowship beginning Monday, January 4, 2027.

The Social Media Fellow is responsible for supporting the creation and distribution of content that drives audience growth and engagement across platforms. They will help us manage our posting schedule, monitor content performance and analytics, tailor posts for specific platforms, and other aspects of audience engagement strategy. The Social Media Fellow must be enthusiastic about reporting the news through social media and video journalism. They should have strong social media management skills and care deeply about reporting news that impacts working people.

Core Responsibilities

• Manage distribution of More Perfect Union content across platforms, ensuring that content is uploaded in a timely manner and is accompanied by engaging copy, titles, alt text, and thumbnails;

• Coordinate with social team members to manage posting schedules and update content calendars;

• Optimize posts for engagement and search, including workshopping and tailoring graphics headlines and video titles/text on screen;

• Run A/B tests, monitor post performance, and make adjustments as needed to maximize reach and viewership;

• Monitor analytics, audience sentiment, and social media trends, and translate learnings into actionable insights for team members on a weekly basis;

• Flag engaging content produced by outlets and creators doing work that is adjacent to MPU or which could inspire the social team to improve its work;

• Engage with our followers by responding to comments, questions, and DMs, directing comments to appropriate team members as needed;

• Complete assignments from supervisor and colleagues and meet deadlines;

• Operate in a nimble environment;

• Other duties as assigned.

Experience/Qualifications

• Demonstrated experience managing social media accounts with a large reach;

• Graphic design and video editing skills, including knowledge of tools such as Canva and CapCut;

• Solid understanding of interfaces, best practices, algorithms, and metrics of major social media platforms, including Instagram, TikTok, Facebook, YouTube, and Twitter/X.

• Familiarity with social media management and analytics tools such as Sprout Social and RivalIQ;

• Avid consumer of news from a variety of sources ranging from mainstream outlets to independent and social media;

• Significant interest in and knowledge of U.S. politics and economic justice issues;

• Excellent written and interpersonal communication skills;

• Exceptional organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage many priorities at once;

• Ability to work independently in a remote, work-from-home environment.

